{title: Far, jeg har syndet}
{subtitle: Luke 15:18–24}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [C] [Dm] | [Bb] [C] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Far off in a foreign land
[C]I sat with [Dm]nothing left
I [Bb]thought about [C]my father's house
And all the good [Dm]I left
I will get up and go to him
And [C]say to him [Dm]today
[Bb]Father, I [C]have sinned against heaven and [Dm]before you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [Bb]ran to meet me on the [F]road
He [C]threw his arms around my [Dm]neck
This [Bb]son of mine was [F]dead and is [C]alive a[Bb]gain
He was lost and is [Dm]found
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I am no longer worthy
[C]To be called [Dm]your son
But [Bb]father called [C]for the best robe
[Dm]A ring upon my hand
And [C]sandals on [Dm]my feet
And the [Bb]feast [C]was all made [Dm]ready
For this [Bb]son [C]of mine was dead and is [Dm]alive
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

